A||||7||Logicdragon||Radar Detectors||||1||
Z||000000||Logicdragon||08-10-2001||11:35 AM||||I've been looking to buy a radar detector but I think mounting them on the windshield or visor looks somewhat tacky.  Does anyone know of a radar detector that can be mounted in the dash and then run some kind of cable with a detection device at the end to the windshield or front grill or something like that.  I want to build a spot in the dash for a radar detector so that it looks like it came stock with the car.  Thanks<P>Logic Dragon   ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||08-10-2001||12:03 PM||||My Brother-in-law has this installed in his Grand Prix. The box can be mounted anywhere and the antennas/sensors can be mounted front and back. He mounted the control box under the lip of the dash.<P>It is made by BEL and works excellent.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.discountcell.com/radar/bel815stir.asp" TARGET=_blank>http://www.discountcell.com/radar/bel815stir.asp</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 08-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Logicdragon||08-10-2001||12:20 PM||||Cool.  That was exactly what I was looking for.  Thanks.<P>Logic Dragon||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||08-10-2001||06:06 PM||||I just used 2 face tape and mounted my bracket at the very top of windshield, ran a hard wire to it. its completely hidden by upper windshield tinting. Tip, they higher you can mount the reciever the more advance warning you get. Just below the roofline will pick one up farther than one in grill or bumper. Works by line of site. same for laser.||||reg||1
Z||000004||bHooper||08-10-2001||06:45 PM||||gotta like K-40!  i ran them for years.  best part is, they will upgrade (or tune) the thing ever so often for $50 (after the waranty has expired)!<P>they aren't cheap (i paid $300 for mine 12 years ago... and they went to $1000 then!)<P>the best installed detector on the market.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.k40.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.k40.com/</A> <P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Red</B></FONT></FONT> 86 GT 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Black</B></FONT> <u>86 SE Automatic</u>||||reg||1
Z||000005||DrDave||08-10-2001||09:29 PM||||I installed one ( a remote model) with the "radar" head just looking thru the crack between the hood and grill on a new dodge P/u.<BR>   The dual inferareds went up behind the  mirror and up behind the drivers head.  The dash mounted ( or ashtray) is just a wee thing. <BR>          Worked lika a charm untill he hit a deer.  Then I used his old grill parts for a template.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Primaris||08-10-2001||11:55 PM||||Check out <A HREF="http://www.radardetectortest.com." TARGET=_blank>www.radardetectortest.com.</A>   Has some good info on detectors.||||reg||1
Z||000007||artherd||08-11-2001||07:35 AM||||I have heard good things about the valentine 1, which has a remote display pannel (optional I belive) as well.  I like it's multi-direcitonal status threat display.<P>Currently deciding between the two.<P>detector, and 13" brakes are on the list before I drop the northstar in :)<BR>(at this rate, I'll never afford it, ho well!)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
